Z||000003||ray b||10-06-2001||12:46 PM||||will a magnet stick to the petal if not replace it,as it is bent, only use a steel petal, not the al alloy one.<BR>ck the bearring at the top side they will wareout but are a quick fix.<BR>then bleed it then bleed it again and one more time bleed it. power sucker works best.<BR>if still a problem ck if G M parts master/slave are used and ck for leaks<P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
Z||000004||Rich86GT||10-06-2001||10:51 PM||||I did some measuring on my '86 GT V6 5 speed.  I crawled under the dash and measured the travel of the clutch rod. The clutch pedal pushed the clutch master cylinder 1.2".  The slave cylinder is slightly larger diameter than the master. The difference in cylinder sizes between the master and slave cylinders allows only a maximum of 1" travel at the slave. If you get 0.9" travel at the slave, your hydraulics are probably fine. ||||reg||1
